 `seed` upserts modules and lessons. Ids derive from slugs, so re-seeding never breaks learner progress. A lesson removed from the Markdown is removed from its module too.
+
+If the database already has a module with the same slug (made in the dashboard, or by an older seed), `seed` skips that module and lists it as a conflict. The Markdown lessons never load, and the site keeps showing the old content. Take the module over with `--chukua`:
+
+```bash
+DATABASE_URL=... pnpm exec tsx scripts/seed.ts --chukua misingi-ya-nuru
+```
+
+The module keeps its id, so classrooms that list it keep working. Progress on an old lesson moves to the new lesson with the same slug. From then on the module belongs to `seed`, and later runs need no flag.
